se access, input validation, JSON encoding into testable functions with clear error handling. Keep external behavior identical: same status codes, same response bodies. Need full refactored file. Need likely define sentinel errors: errInvalidID, errUserNotFound, errDatabase? But external behavior: 400 body {\"error\":\"bad id\"} no Content-Type? Original 400/404/500 do not set Content-Type. Success sets Content-Type application/json and encodes map. JSON encoder adds newline. Need preserve exact bodies? \"same response bodies\" likely exact bytes. For success, json.Encoder.Encode(map[string]string{\"name\": name, \"email\": email}) produces {\"email\":\"...\",\"name\":\"...\"}\\n because Go map keys sorted alphabetically. Need preserve. If we use json.Marshal(map[string]string{...}) and w.Write, no newline. That would change body. Need use json.NewEncoder(w).Encode or ensure newline. Better keep encoding/json Encoder for success. But", "top2": [[[1596, -0.0026298740413039923], [760, -6.9340434074401855]], [[1144, -1.3828373084834311e-05], [14235, -12.044021606445312]], [[4087, -0.013323456980288029], [310, -4.498484134674072]], [[1156, -0.040906645357608795], [303, -3.3838460445404053]], [[579, -0.22416292130947113], [25, -2.3427751064300537]], [[1622, -0.003230718430131674], [3296, -6.490668773651123]], [[13, -0.3306863605976105], [25, -1.6506212949752808]], [[14235, -0.0330643430352211], [1165, -4.182968616485596]], [[89109, -0.3148415982723236], [7936, -1.8629792928695679]], [[5805, -0.00022491361596621573], [2400, -8.784971237182617]], [[9830, -0.023366307839751244], [6795, -3.8262112140655518]], [[6795, -2.801457594614476e-05], [17369, -11.926827430725098]], [[1083, -1.4167749881744385], [47781, -1.5785659551620483]], [[1228, -0.10444477200508118], [2400, -2.7177011966705322]], [[470, -3.1352534278994426e-05], [5568, -10.649325370788574]], [[5568, -0.0028676341753453016], [74243, -6.170428276062012]], [[440, -0.9206647276878357], [25, -1.8649128675460815]], [[2